# SQL migrations are checksummed by sqlx (sha384 of the exact bytes) and
# the checksum is stored in `_sqlx_migrations` when a migration is
# applied. With core.autocrlf, a branch switch can rewrite a migration's
# line endings, and the app then refuses to start ("migration N was
# previously applied but has been modified"). Pin every migration's line
# endings to the bytes it was originally applied with:
#   0001–0011 were applied with CRLF, 0012 and 0013 with LF.
# New migrations: add an explicit line here (prefer eol=lf).
src-tauri/migrations/*.sql text eol=crlf
src-tauri/migrations/0012_pane_lines_unique.sql text eol=lf
src-tauri/migrations/0013_servers_drop_mock_stats.sql text eol=lf
